# Flutter Component Revision Page — `Icon`

## 1. What is `Icon`?

`Icon` is a Flutter widget used to display **small graphical symbols**.

Examples:

* Home 🏠
* Search 🔍
* Settings ⚙️
* Heart ❤️
* Profile 👤
* Delete 🗑️
* Menu ☰

Flutter provides many built-in Material icons.

---

# 2. Basic Syntax

```dart
Icon(Icons.home)
```

Example:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: Center(
    child: Icon(Icons.home),
  ),
)
```

---

# 3. `Icons`

`Icons` contains Flutter's built-in Material icons.

Examples:

```dart
Icons.home
Icons.search
Icons.settings
Icons.person
Icons.favorite
Icons.delete
Icons.add
Icons.close
Icons.menu
Icons.arrow_back
Icons.arrow_forward
Icons.email
Icons.phone
Icons.shopping_cart
```

You don't put quotes around the icon name.

Correct:

```dart
Icon(Icons.home)
```

Not:

```dart
Icon("home")
```

---

# 4. Changing Icon Size

Use:

```dart
size:
```

Example:

```dart
Icon(
  Icons.home,
  size: 40,
)
```

The default size is commonly around 24 logical pixels.

---

# 5. Changing Icon Color

Use:

```dart
color:
```

Example:

```dart
Icon(
  Icons.favorite,
  color: Colors.red,
)
```

You can combine size and color:

```dart
Icon(
  Icons.favorite,
  size: 35,
  color: Colors.red,
)
```

---

# 6. Icon Inside a Row

Very common in app development.

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Icon(Icons.person),
    SizedBox(width: 10),
    Text("John"),
  ],
)
```

Result:

```text
👤  John
```

Common uses:

* Profile information
* Settings
* Contact details
* Menu items
* List items

---

# 7. Icon Inside an AppBar

Icons are extremely common in `AppBar`.

```dart
AppBar(
  title: Text("Home"),
  actions: [
    Icon(Icons.search),
    Icon(Icons.more_vert),
  ],
)
```

Usually, however, interactive icons should be placed inside `IconButton`.

```dart
AppBar(
  title: Text("Home"),
  actions: [
    IconButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      icon: Icon(Icons.search),
    ),
  ],
)
```

---

# 8. `Icon` vs `IconButton`

This distinction is important.

### `Icon`

Only **displays** the icon.

```dart
Icon(Icons.delete)
```

### `IconButton`

Displays an icon that the user can **tap**.

```dart
IconButton(
  onPressed: () {
    print("Delete clicked");
  },
  icon: Icon(Icons.delete),
)
```

### Remember

```text
Icon       → visual
IconButton → clickable icon
```

---

# 9. IconButton Example

```dart
IconButton(
  onPressed: () {
    print("Search clicked");
  },
  icon: Icon(Icons.search),
)
```

When the user taps the icon, the code inside `onPressed` runs.

---

# 10. Real-World Example — Music Player

A music player may have:

```dart
Row(
  mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
  children: [
    IconButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      icon: Icon(Icons.skip_previous),
    ),

    IconButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      icon: Icon(Icons.play_arrow),
    ),

    IconButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      icon: Icon(Icons.skip_next),
    ),
  ],
)
```

Conceptually:

```text
     ⏮       ▶       ⏭
```

---

# 11. Icon + Text

A very common UI pattern:

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Icon(Icons.email),
    SizedBox(width: 8),
    Text("user@gmail.com"),
  ],
)
```

Result:

```text
✉  user@gmail.com
```

This pattern appears in:

* Profile screens
* Contact pages
* Settings
* User information
* Product details

---

# 12. Icon in a Button

Example:

```dart
ElevatedButton.icon(
  onPressed: () {},
  icon: Icon(Icons.login),
  label: Text("Login"),
)
```

Result:

```text
[ 🔑 Login ]
```

This is usually better than manually putting an icon and button together.

---

# 13. Icon in a Container

You can style the area around an icon using `Container`.

```dart
Container(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(12),
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: Colors.blue,
    shape: BoxShape.circle,
  ),
  child: Icon(
    Icons.person,
    color: Colors.white,
  ),
)
```

This can create a circular icon background.

---

# 14. Important Icon Properties

The commonly used properties are:

```dart
Icon(
  Icons.home,
  size: 30,
  color: Colors.blue,
  semanticLabel: "Home",
)
```

### `size`

Controls icon size.

### `color`

Controls icon color.

### `semanticLabel`

Provides a description useful for accessibility.

